<Layout
  title="Website SEO & Index Checker Privacy Policy"
  description="How Website SEO & Index Checker handles public audits, site crawling, optional Google indexing and PageSpeed, saved checks, retention and deletion."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy / Website SEO &amp; Index Checker</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy — <em>Website SEO &amp; Index Checker</em></h1>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> November 26, 2026<br /><strong>Developer:</strong> Velvet &amp; Pixel<br /><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a></p>

    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Website SEO &amp; Index Checker, formerly called IndexPilot, is an Android utility for auditing public website pages, crawling a bounded portion of a site, and understanding Google's recorded indexing information. This policy covers the Android app, including testing builds. The existing <code>/privacy/indexpilot/</code> address remains its privacy-policy URL.</p>
    <p>Public page audits and site crawls do not require a Velvet &amp; Pixel account or Google sign-in. Search Console features require separate authorization through Google. Optional PageSpeed analysis sends the selected public page URL to Google without requiring Search Console access. Velvet &amp; Pixel does not operate an app backend that receives your audit URLs, page contents or reports.</p>
    <p>The app reports observations and suggested improvements; it does not change your website or deploy files. Future paid features, scheduled monitoring or website-editing services are not part of the current app and would require updated disclosures where applicable.</p>

    <h2>Public page audits and site crawling</h2>
    <p>When you start a page audit, the app sends requests directly from your device to that website and supporting public resources, such as robots.txt and sitemap files. Depending on the check, following redirects or sitemap references can contact other public hosts. The app temporarily reads response headers, page HTML, robots rules and sitemap XML to generate findings. Raw response bodies are not saved in the workflow database.</p>
    <p>If you choose a site crawl, the app also discovers and checks public HTML pages within the selected website origin and folder. The crawl is limited to 50 HTML pages, with additional discovery, time and data limits. It checks robots rules and can save page URLs, response status, titles, descriptions, link references, findings, progress and partial results. It does not execute website JavaScript, sign in to websites or promise to discover every page.</p>
    <p>Website operators and their hosting providers can receive normal request information, including requested paths and query strings, your device's network IP address, request timing and the app's user-agent string. They handle their own logs under their policies. Public website requests do not include your Google access token or your browser's signed-in cookies.</p>
    <p>The app accepts public HTTP and HTTPS websites. HTTP requests are not encrypted and can be visible to network intermediaries; HTTPS requests use encrypted transport with certificate validation. Do not enter URLs containing private access keys, personal information or other secrets. Public audits do not require website ownership or access to private pages.</p>

    <h2>Optional Google Search Console access</h2>
    <p>Google authorization is handled by Google Play services and Google's consent interface. Website SEO &amp; Index Checker requests the read-only Search Console permission, <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/webmasters.readonly</code>, to discover properties available to the authorized account and inspect a URL covered by a property. It does not ask for or receive your Google password or request access to Gmail, Drive files, contacts or payment details.</p>
    <p>Google can return property URLs and permission levels, recorded indexing and coverage states, last-crawl information, robots and fetch states, canonical URLs, and reported sitemap or referring-page URLs. The app uses this information to display diagnostics and next steps and retain your checks. An inspection sends the entered URL and selected property identifier to Google's Search Console API over HTTPS. This retrieves recorded information; it is not Google's live URL test or an indexing request.</p>
    <p>The app does not save access tokens or refresh tokens in its database or preferences and does not request offline server access. Short-lived authorization results are used in memory. Google Play services manages its own authorization and token cache and may retain a grant so it can supply access again. Closing a check or deleting local reports does not itself revoke that grant.</p>
    <p>Website SEO &amp; Index Checker's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements. We do not sell Google user data, use it for advertising or transfer it to a developer-operated analytics service. Google processes authorization, API requests and related technical information under its own policies.</p>

    <h2>Optional Google PageSpeed analysis</h2>
    <p>Before a PageSpeed analysis, the app explains that the selected public page URL will be sent to Google and asks you to continue. Google receives that URL, including any path and query string, and normal service-request information such as your device's network IP address. Google may fetch and render the public page in its own browser to produce a mobile Lighthouse analysis. Google can receive the URL even if quota or another error prevents a completed analysis.</p>
    <p>This request is separate from Search Console authorization. The app does not send your Search Console token, Google password or signed-in website cookies to PageSpeed. It does not send your other saved checks or upload the app's local report database. No Google sign-in is required by the app for this API request.</p>
    <p>When available, the app receives category scores, lab metrics, the analyzed page URL and improvement recommendations. It saves selected results, observation times and status messages with the relevant check. It does not retain the full raw Lighthouse response or its screenshots. Availability depends on Google's service, quota and the app build's configuration; a failed analysis does not create passing scores or erase your other reports.</p>
    <p>If you choose <strong>Open PageSpeed</strong>, your browser opens Google's PageSpeed website with the selected page URL. Your browser and Google then handle that visit, including any browser-managed cookies, under their own settings and policies.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention">Google data retention information</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Manage Google Account connections</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Local storage and saved checks</h2>
    <p>The app stores an active workflow and up to 20 saved checks in Android application-private storage. Records can contain entered and final page URLs, operation states, observation times, public SEO findings and evidence, discovered sitemap URLs, crawl progress and results, selected PageSpeed results, Search Console property information and recorded Google inspection results. URLs, query strings and diagnostic evidence can themselves be sensitive.</p>
    <p>Checks with recorded results can remain in <strong>Saved checks</strong> when you start another page or recheck an earlier page. As new checks are saved, older entries can be removed to keep the history within its limit. Reopening a saved report shows its stored observations; it does not automatically fetch fresh data. There is no cloud synchronization or scheduled monitoring.</p>
    <p>Appearance choices, including accent and theme, are stored separately as local preferences. Local records remain until you clear them, they are displaced by the saved-check limit, or the app's storage is removed. The app does not apply a separate timed expiry to saved reports.</p>

    <h2>Your deletion and Google-access controls</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Clear current results</strong> removes the active check, including its SEO, crawl, PageSpeed and Google indexing results, and its matching entry in Saved checks. Other saved checks and appearance preferences remain. This does not revoke your Google permission.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete all saved checks</strong> removes the saved-check history and active workflow from this app. Appearance preferences and any Google-managed authorization grant are not removed by this action.</li>
      <li><strong>Disconnect and clear Google results</strong> removes saved Search Console property and indexing information across the active workflow and saved checks, while keeping public SEO, crawl and PageSpeed reports. It also attempts to revoke the app's Google authorization. If Google cannot confirm revocation, the app directs you to Google Account connections settings, where you can remove access yourself.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Local deletion does not delete your website, Search Console property, Google's records or logs already held by website and service providers. Those providers control their own retention. Google Play services retains its own authorization data under Google's controls.</p>
    <p>Clearing the app's storage in Android Settings or uninstalling removes its private workflow, history and preferences. The app excludes its ordinary local storage from Android cloud backup and device transfer. It does not add a separate encryption layer to the database or preferences; protection relies on Android's app sandbox and device security.</p>

    <h2>Advertising, purchases and technical information</h2>
    <p>The current app has no billing integration, advertising SDK, developer-operated analytics or crash-reporting service. A promotions icon lets you choose to browse Velvet &amp; Pixel's apps in your browser; it does not automatically open that website or transmit your audit results to it.</p>
    <p>Google Play services may process technical and diagnostic information needed for authorization and related services, such as app, device, network and operation information. Google determines its handling and retention of that information. Connection help can copy technical app/setup diagnostics for you to share with support; it does not include your password, access token or Google account details.</p>
    <p>Internet access supports public website checks, optional Google APIs and user-selected external links. The app does not request access to your photos, contacts, microphone or precise location.</p>

    <h2>Support and external links</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we receive your email address and the information you choose to include. We use it to answer your request and retain correspondence while needed for support or applicable obligations. Avoid sending passwords, access tokens or confidential Search Console information. Contact us to ask about deletion of support correspondence we hold.</p>
    <p>Opening Search Console, PageSpeed, this policy or studio promotional links uses your browser and the destination's privacy practices. This policy and the studio website are hosted on GitHub Pages, which receives normal website requests when you visit. Following an external link does not automatically attach your saved audit report.</p>

    <h2>Children's privacy and security</h2>
    <p>Website SEO &amp; Index Checker is a general-purpose website utility and is not specifically designed for children. We do not knowingly solicit children's personal information through the app. If you believe a child has supplied personal information directly to Velvet &amp; Pixel, contact us so we can address it. Google account services operate under Google's policies.</p>
    <p>The app uses Android private storage, Google-provided authorization and HTTPS for Google API calls. Public fetching is bounded and rejects local or private network destinations. These safeguards do not change the privacy practices of websites you audit or external services you choose.</p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy as functionality, integrations or requirements change. The effective date appears above. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:velvetandpixel@gmail.com">velvetandpixel@gmail.com</a>.</p>
